{
  "abstract": "A Lean 4 / Mathlib proof that a finite simple graph G has a total colouring with Δ(G) + 2 colours (a map on V ⊕ E(G) giving different colours to adjacent vertices, to distinct edges with a common endpoint, and to incident vertex–edge pairs) in three situations: (1) tcc_of_independent: G has an independent set S with |V| ≤ |S| + Δ + 1 (Yap–Wang–Zhang 1989, Lemma 2.2; Yap–Chew 1992, Lemma 2.4); (2) tcc_of_card_le_maxDegree_add_three: Δ(G) ≥ |V| − 3 (Yap–Wang–Zhang 1989, Theorem 2.3 and the closing remarks); (3) tcc_of_card_le_maxDegree_add_four: Δ(G) ≥ |V| − 4, for every finite simple graph (no further hypothesis; Yap–Wang–Zhang 1989, Theorem 2.4). The proofs use Yap's apex-vertex technique: a new vertex joined to the vertices outside one or two independent pairs, matchings found by the enlarge-matching argument (when Δ ≥ 7 or G has three pairwise non-adjacent vertices) or, when G has no three pairwise non-adjacent vertices, the two alternating matchings of a Hamiltonian path through the vertices outside the pairs, and Fournier's theorem (PALOMAR-2026-11-08-000009) or Vizing's theorem (PALOMAR-2026-10-15-000004), both imported as lake dependencies, in place of the Chetwynd–Hilton theorem on three vertices of maximum degree and Kostochka's theorem for Δ ≤ 4 used in the original paper.",
